dict(id='G40', act=8, card="Your Wallet", sub="Three lessons"),
dict(id='G41', act=8, set='cork7', vis='Corkboard, three index cards pinned one by one.',
  lines=[('N', "You don't need to own a single game share for this story to matter to your money. Three things to take from it."),
         ('N', "One. Check how much of your money rides on one thing. Priya's shares lost close to a tenth in a day because of one date. If one company, one product or one stock is a big part of what you own, a single headline can move your whole net worth. Index funds spread that risk across hundreds of companies. That's not a tip. It's just how risk works."),
         ('N', "Two. The good news is usually already in the price. By launch day, everyone knew this would be huge. Markets try to price in what everyone already knows, which is why the biggest launch ever, and the stock went up, are not the same sentence."),
         ('N', "Three. Watch the twenty-dollar nudge. Nine in ten early buyers chose the more expensive edition. That's not a crime. It's a great product. But the upgrade button works on everything, from phones to flights to fries. Decide your fun budget before the shop decides it for you.")]),
